{SungTae Moon} received his B.S. degree from Chonnam National University, Gwangju, South Korea, in 2005; his M.S. degree from the Gwangju Institute of Science and Technology (GIST), Gwangju, South Korea, in 2007; and his Ph.D. degree in aeronautical engineering from KAIST in 2021. From 2007 to 2010, he was at the Agency for Defense Development (ADD), where he developed a mission computer for aircraft. From 2011 to 2012, he was at the National Security Research Institute (NSRI) and worked in the area of security in embedded systems. From 2012 to 2022, he has been a senior researcher with the artificial intelligence research division of the Korea Aerospace Research Institute (KARI). Since 2022, he has been with Korea University of Technology and Education(KOREATECH), Cheonan, South Korea, where he is currently an assistant professor in the School of Computer Science and Engineering. His current research interests include swarming flight system, navigation algorithm, and object detection based on deep learning.
